YAAP: 63-cdi-cav-gno-fem-neu ... or why I like glass
****

I've been on a bit of a hot streak recently.  This game marks my 7th
ascension over my last 11 games (and 3rd in a row).  The grand tour is
also proceeding apace.  This marks the 21st different starting role-
race-alignment combination (of 38 possible) I've ascended.

I didn't set out with any specific conduct/stylish weapon goals.  I
set out to win.  This is also the first game where I made methodical
use of a unicorn horn to #dip-test potions.  I'm still learning a new
trick or three each game.

Throughout the game I played current weapon hot-potato, swapping
between assorted artifacts (the +6 Scepter, the +6 Sunsword, the +2
Excalibur, the +0 Vorpal Blade) and my trusty +2 sling.  Once I'd
sorted the gems from the glass, I kept the glass ... as ammunition.
It's light, it's plentiful, and if it breaks ... you don't care.

The early game was very favorable.  Dlvl.02 had a large, mimic free,
scroll shop.  There was enough ?identify to get my club to +7.
Getting the money to buy them all took some time.  Just below the
Oracle, my path to Sokoban was blocked by a crocodile and a werewolf.
I hadn't cleaned out the scroll shop yet, so I left for safer ground.

A hobbit dropped a cloak of displacement in the first level of the
mines, so I decided to do a displacement game and never acquired
permanent invisibility.  Minetown had a bag of holding.  Feeling
tougher, I went back towards sokoban.  Sokoban was the bag of holding
version ... boo!  Seeing a peaceful grey unicorn on the way back made
everything worthwhile.

I played ring rental with the shopkeeper on Dlvl.4 ... going back and
forth a few times to get just one ring I needed (fire resistance for
dealing with a red Naga, for example) while selling those I didn't
need.

A magic lamp from the bottom half of the mines netted a djinni wish
(hello +2 grey dragon scale mail).  Mines end was the catacombs, which
seems to fit my luck (my spellcasters usually get something else).  I
also came across a bones pile with an amulet of reflection and
Excalibur.  Team 'q' got xkraelx, while helpless.

Just below medusa's swamp, team Polytrap turned the minotaur hovering
near the stairs into something harmless (queen bee).  Medusa had
everything (scimitar, shield, boots, *and* the sack).  The castle was
easy, mainly due to drawbridge concerto and conflict.  The castle wand
was (0:3), HURRAY!  The armoury had Sunsword, and I *like* Sunsword.

The quest was a sleepwalk, the Chromatic Dragon didn't even summon
nasties.

There's a noticeable difference between doing the VoTD with MC2 and
MC3.  I was level-drained a few times, nothing major though.  While
clearing out Orcus-town, stethoscope testing revealed that Sunsword
doesn't get base damage or enchantment damage against shades.  This, I
think, is a bug.

Beelzebub and Asmodeus were paid off, as usual, for less than 10gp
each.  Killing Orcus didn't involve anything unexpected.  I was
chasing a teleporting lich up the dungeon when I arrived at Juiblex
swamp.  I killed Juiblex without leaving the downstair (again, as
usual).

The ascension run was uneventful until I reached the planes ... then
things got interesting.  I was engulfed *nine times* on the plane of
air, 7 times by air elementals and twice by vortices.

The first AE was killed via sleep+melee (from inside).  This, I
realized, was a losing plan.  The second was teleported away.  Then
came a foo-vortex.  The next engulf (#4, and I hadn't moved more than
5 spaces from where I arrived) resulted in a wish for a blessed
greased tooled horn.  To paraphrase billnye, it does soothe the savage
beast.

The Astral plane was an agonizingly long (by my standards) 3-altar
tour.  I managed to empty all three of my wands of teleportation in
the process (and had to take time charging them), and wound up
breaking one towards the end.  The endgame involved much more drama
than I'm comfortable with.

-cdi

